  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Al-Maqmu&apos;een</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Al-Maqmu&apos;een is an independent social media platform based in Tunisia, designed to empower young people by strengthening their participation in decision-making, policy development, and implementation. The initiative seeks to create a trusted, transparent, and inclusive space for Tunisian youth, offering them access to reliable information and the opportunity to actively engage in the country&apos;s political and civic discourse. Through this platform, young voices will be better equipped to influence policies, contribute to societal change, and shape Tunisia&apos;s future.

&quot;Al-Maqmu&apos;een&quot; offers explainer videos, podcasts, and satire to empower youth with reliable information and a platform for free expression. Objectives include raising political awareness, amplifying marginalized voices, and fostering inclusive dialogue. The project aims to boost youth engagement in civic life.

The project targets youth, particularlymarginalized groups like political activists and youth from underserved areas. These beneficiaries will gain access to a platform for voicing their opinions and participating in national conversations.

The project will empower youth by providing them with a platform to engage in political and social discussions, amplifying marginalized voices and promoting informed civic participation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BESIYESSAH</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Be-Siyessah is a dynamic digital media platform dedicated to empowering young Arab speakers, especially in the MENA region. The platform focuses on producing content that addresses key social issues, promotes inclusivity, and fosters community engagement.

Board of Directors: The board includes individuals with expertise in media, social issues, and community engagement. It guides the strategic direction of the organization and ensures that the mission aligns with the needs of young, marginalized communities.

Executive Team: Led by the Co-founder and CEO, the executive team oversees day-to-day operations and ensures that social impact remains centralto Be-Siyessah&#x2019;s work.

Staff: Be-Siyessah employs diverse staff members from different backgrounds, including those from marginalized groups, to ensure that the perspectives of these communities are represented in the content and projects created.

Be-Siyessah actively involves marginalized groups in several ways:

Targeting Content: The content produced directly addresses issues affecting marginalized communities, including racial and ethnic minorities, economically disadvantaged groups, and migrants, ensuring these voices are heard.

Staff and Board Representation: The organization prioritizes hiring individuals from marginalized groups, fostering an inclusive work environment that reflects the diversity of the communities served.

Community Engagement: Be-Siyessah engages marginalized groups through participatory campaigns and content creation, giving them a platform to share their stories and experiences.

Marginalized groups often lack equal access to resources, representation, and opportunities, and Be-Siyessah works to amplify their voices and address the inequities they face.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
